WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.300
Will she put poison in it?

00:00:03.623 --> 00:00:04.922
I didn’t say anything.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:05.842
What?

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:07.530
What kind of drink would you want?

00:00:07.551 --> 00:00:08.392
I want something strong.

00:00:08.411 --> 00:00:09.342
-Something strong?
-Yes.

00:00:09.364 --> 00:00:10.788
Like this?

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:11.485
I want something strong.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.200
These are not white roses.

00:00:14.444 --> 00:00:15.413
What are they?

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.219
-It made me feel spirited.
-Right?

00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:17.955
Yes.

00:00:17.985 --> 00:00:21.931
It’s like having a kitten.

00:00:21.957 --> 00:00:23.158
A kitten?

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.610
[WELCOME TO MOONSHADOW VLOG EP.2]

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.390
-Is it recording?
-It’s been recording for a while.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.254
Okay.

00:00:31.277 --> 00:00:34.697
Today, I’m going to work
as a bartender for Key.

00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:36.699
Key, what kind of drink do you want?

00:00:36.764 --> 00:00:38.797
I want a light alcoholic drink.
I’m a lightweight.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.160
You want a light alcoholic drink?

00:00:41.426 --> 00:00:42.859
Yes. Is it P’Chan’s recipe?

00:00:42.882 --> 00:00:43.497
Yes.

00:00:43.521 --> 00:00:45.312
Will I get drunk after drinking it?

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.321
It’s a non-alcoholic mocktail.

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:50.080
It’s perfect for Key’s sweet style.

00:00:50.108 --> 00:00:51.112
Alright.

00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:52.973
-I’ll get started.
-Is it going to be edible?

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.306
Will she put poison in it?

00:00:54.337 --> 00:00:55.601
I didn’t say anything.

00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:56.568
What?

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.002
Hello, Miss.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:58.524
Hi.

00:00:58.542 --> 00:01:00.010
What kind of drink would you want?

00:01:00.035 --> 00:01:00.887
I want something strong.

00:01:00.911 --> 00:01:02.096
-Something strong?
-Yes.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.142
-Like this?
-I want something strong.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.198
I haven’t hit you yet.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.346
[THE IMPACT HIT THE PERSON NEXT TO HER.]

00:01:08.346 --> 00:01:09.590
They could feel the impact too.
[THE IMPACT HIT THE PERSON NEXT TO HER.]

00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:11.590
This is too strong.

00:01:12.297 --> 00:01:13.512
I want something strong, Key.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.632
Something strong?

00:01:14.656 --> 00:01:16.585
-So strong that it can knock me out.
-Knock you out?

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:18.411
Like this?

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.920
[WHEN WILL THEY EVER GET THE DRINK?]

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.106
I’ll make a strong drink for you.
[WHEN WILL THEY EVER GET THE DRINK?]

00:01:22.394 --> 00:01:23.536
-You want a strong drink?
-Yes.

00:01:23.558 --> 00:01:24.979
Something strong that will hit you?
[A STRONG COCKTAIL.]

00:01:25.008 --> 00:01:26.047
-Like Sun’s personality?
-Yes.

00:01:26.195 --> 00:01:28.050
You can drop your act, Jay.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.050
I know you hate me.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.050
[MOONSHADOW VLOG]

00:01:34.303 --> 00:01:38.531
The drink that I will make for Bonnie
will be light

00:01:38.589 --> 00:01:41.106
because that’s what she requested.

00:01:41.251 --> 00:01:44.402
These are the ingredients.

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:47.589
I want it to be a bit sour,
like passion fruit.

00:01:47.614 --> 00:01:48.928
But I’m not sure if she will like it.

00:01:48.976 --> 00:01:49.870
Okay.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:51.925
We need a glass.
[THE BARTENDER WHO WILL INSTRUCT CHAN.]

00:01:52.401 --> 00:01:54.671
First, I’ll put a lemon slice in it.

00:01:55.112 --> 00:01:56.373
Two pieces of cucumber.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.000
I’ll add lime juice.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.570
[ADD CUCUMBER SYRUP]

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.748
Bonnie likes vegetables.

00:02:00.896 --> 00:02:02.146
-Do I add the whole glass?
-Yes.
[PINEAPPLE AND PASSION FRUIT JUICE]

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.263
Okay.
[PINEAPPLE AND PASSION FRUIT JUICE]

00:02:03.506 --> 00:02:04.576
Is it done?

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:06.291
Please wait a bit longer.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:08.589
There.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.770
[ADD SPARKLING WATER]

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.942
I’ll put a piece of passion fruit here.

00:02:12.976 --> 00:02:16.465
The drink for Key is ready.

00:02:16.497 --> 00:02:17.691
It’s sour and fizzy.

00:02:20.922 --> 00:02:22.598
Here is your drink.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:22.958
[YOU SCARED ME.
YOU NEED TO GIVE ME A HUG.]

00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:24.414
I was zoning out.
[YOU SCARED ME.
YOU NEED TO GIVE ME A HUG.]

00:02:24.414 --> 00:02:25.270
[YOU SCARED ME.
YOU NEED TO GIVE ME A HUG.]

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:29.634
The drink is made of
passion fruit juice, lemon, and…

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:30.285
What?

00:02:30.315 --> 00:02:30.888
Lemon.

00:02:30.909 --> 00:02:32.220
It also has cucumber.

00:02:32.242 --> 00:02:33.788
-Cucumber?
-Yes, cucumber.

00:02:34.001 --> 00:02:35.288
Will I get drunk after drinking it?

00:02:35.311 --> 00:02:37.400
No, it’s non-alcoholic.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.099
How is it?

00:02:40.554 --> 00:02:44.499
-It has a strong cucumber aroma.
-Yes, I know that you like vegetables.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.102
But I never said
I like a drink with a vegetable aroma.

00:02:48.063 --> 00:02:49.746
How is it? Give it a review.

00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:51.450
Besides the aroma, it’s pretty good.

00:02:51.528 --> 00:02:54.077
I like it. It’s refreshing.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.097
I want to eat this.

00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:00.161
I’ll help stir it.

00:03:00.377 --> 00:03:01.807
-Will you drink it too?
-Yes.

00:03:01.998 --> 00:03:03.562
Let me taste it after I stir it.

00:03:04.632 --> 00:03:05.717
I like it.

00:03:05.746 --> 00:03:06.997
I’ll give it to you.

00:03:07.528 --> 00:03:09.622
Key, don’t you like the drink
that I made for you?

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:13.908
It’s tasty, but I don’t mind
giving delicious food to someone I love.

00:03:13.936 --> 00:03:14.792
Really?

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.090
[I DON’T MIND GIVING DELICIOUS FOOD
TO SOMEONE I LOVE.]

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:18.749
[KEY WILL START TO MAKE THE DRINK]

00:03:18.749 --> 00:03:20.743
(This drink is called Lychee Rush.)
[KEY WILL START TO MAKE THE DRINK]

00:03:20.762 --> 00:03:21.989
Lychee Rush.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.588
(We will use guava juice.)

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:25.711
Guava juice.

00:03:28.081 --> 00:03:28.847
Please wait a moment.

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.202
Sure.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.670
[GRAPE JUICE]

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.657
Okay.

00:03:33.891 --> 00:03:35.400
(Add ice.)

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.668
Does it contain alcohol?

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.167
No.

00:03:39.463 --> 00:03:40.497
(Shake it like this.)

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.534
Wait.
[READY TO SHAKE.]

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:42.565
[READY TO SHAKE.]

00:03:42.565 --> 00:03:44.069
Do you have a spare shirt?
[READY TO SHAKE.]

00:03:45.517 --> 00:03:46.561
(You can shake it harder.)

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.950
[SHAKE IT HARD TO MAKE IT DELICIOUS.]

00:03:49.453 --> 00:03:51.070
I need to shake it hard
to make it delicious.

00:03:51.666 --> 00:03:54.597
This is perfect for Key.

00:03:58.291 --> 00:04:00.068
(It looks like you are making Somtam.)

00:04:01.204 --> 00:04:02.397
Really?

00:04:03.182 --> 00:04:04.293
Why do you see it that way?

00:04:04.331 --> 00:04:07.395
You said you want something strong.

00:04:07.592 --> 00:04:09.902
So I need to shake it hard
to make a tasty drink.

00:04:10.408 --> 00:04:11.798
Shake it hard.

00:04:13.287 --> 00:04:14.925
-(Are you tired?)
-Yes.

00:04:14.958 --> 00:04:16.531
Look, I got muscles.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.435
(You open it by hitting it.)

00:04:18.468 --> 00:04:19.360
Hit it?

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.201
(Like this.)

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.100
(Show your skill.)

00:04:23.614 --> 00:04:24.899
(It will come off.)

00:04:32.537 --> 00:04:34.974
It looks so tasty.

00:04:35.173 --> 00:04:37.367
I’ll add sparkling water.

00:04:37.521 --> 00:04:40.365
(You’ll top it with a lychee
coated with burnt sugar.)

00:04:40.397 --> 00:04:41.887
That’s so cool.

00:04:41.911 --> 00:04:43.688
I want to drink it myself.

00:04:44.099 --> 00:04:45.945
Don’t you like the drink
that I made for you?

00:04:45.977 --> 00:04:46.902
I’m sad.

00:04:46.922 --> 00:04:48.404
Okay.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.447
Let’s serve this to P’Chan.

00:04:51.386 --> 00:04:53.202
The lychee is coated with burnt sugar.

00:04:53.896 --> 00:04:55.548
I’m afraid it might have poison in it.
I’ll taste it for you.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:56.900
Okay.

00:04:59.062 --> 00:04:59.847
How is it?

00:05:00.506 --> 00:05:01.900
Is it sweet? Is it delicious?

00:05:03.282 --> 00:05:04.202
I like this drink.

00:05:04.724 --> 00:05:06.708
I like them both.
But I like this one more.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:07.896
I like this one.

00:05:11.158 --> 00:05:12.460
We should have made our own drink.

00:05:12.481 --> 00:05:14.023
You’re right.

00:05:14.374 --> 00:05:16.700
Thank you for making our own drink.

00:05:16.802 --> 00:05:18.728
Yes, thank you for making our own drink.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.730
It’s delicious. It’s very refreshing.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:24.631
-Are you talking about my drink?
-No, mine.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.807
I think my drink is very delicious.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.400
-Let’s clink our glasses.
-We have our own preferences.

00:05:29.908 --> 00:05:30.814
Here.

00:05:40.909 --> 00:05:43.485
These are flowers that we will use.

00:05:43.754 --> 00:05:44.945
That’s right.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:49.309
I’ll choose a vase for Key.

00:05:49.413 --> 00:05:51.571
Key, which vase will you choose for me?

00:05:51.605 --> 00:05:53.571
I think you should use a small vase.

00:05:53.989 --> 00:05:55.899
I’ll pick this small one.

00:05:56.619 --> 00:05:57.120
Right?

00:05:57.142 --> 00:05:58.475
Bonnie, you should use this one.

00:05:58.503 --> 00:06:02.469
Are you serious?

00:06:02.714 --> 00:06:03.899
I’ll pick this one.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.096
How about this one?

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:10.320
-Is it too big?
-I want a big one.

00:06:10.343 --> 00:06:13.468
See? I pick the one that she likes.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.201
They are so different.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:15.779
[THEIR SIZES ARE DIFFERENT.]

00:06:15.779 --> 00:06:17.127
This one is for P’Mi.
[THEIR SIZES ARE DIFFERENT.]

00:06:21.068 --> 00:06:23.656
How should we start?
Should we start from the big one?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:24.805
It’s up to us.

00:06:24.832 --> 00:06:27.051
It’s an art. There’s no right or wrong.

00:06:27.277 --> 00:06:32.188
-What flower should I choose for Key?
-P’Chan is Key’s pure love.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:33.580
So I will use white roses.
[WHITE ROSES MEAN PURE LOVE, HONESTY,
RESPECT, AND A NEW BEGINNING.]

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:33.602
[WHITE ROSES MEAN PURE LOVE, HONESTY,
RESPECT, AND A NEW BEGINNING.]

00:06:33.602 --> 00:06:35.051
There’s a meaning behind it.
[WHITE ROSES MEAN PURE LOVE, HONESTY,
RESPECT, AND A NEW BEGINNING.]

00:06:35.281 --> 00:06:37.801
These are not white roses.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.099
What are they?

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:40.614
They are not roses.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.521
Aren’t they roses?

00:06:42.546 --> 00:06:43.605
No.

00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:45.585
But they look similar.

00:06:45.619 --> 00:06:47.044
They look similar, right?

00:06:47.069 --> 00:06:48.303
Yes.

00:06:49.158 --> 00:06:51.297
I’ll use this flower.

00:06:51.327 --> 00:06:54.897
Because Key is my sunshine.

00:06:55.268 --> 00:06:58.524
Its color is similar to sunlight.

00:06:58.543 --> 00:07:00.524
It’s ombre.

00:07:00.749 --> 00:07:03.352
♪ Slowly let your feelings run free ♪

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:07.008
♪ You’ll remember no one else but me ♪

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.400
-P’Chan, did you pick the flowers?
-I’m almost done.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:15.801
Oh my.

00:07:16.644 --> 00:07:19.063
It’s so pretty that it doesn’t look real.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.318
So cute, P’Chan.

00:07:21.343 --> 00:07:23.974
P’Chan, you will love Key.

00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:25.374
Here.

00:07:25.405 --> 00:07:26.503
(It’s cute.)

00:07:29.022 --> 00:07:32.780
I want Key to feel more cheerful.

00:07:32.811 --> 00:07:36.431
So I chose yellow and orange flowers.

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:38.248
They are ombre.

00:07:38.271 --> 00:07:41.365
Just like Key said earlier,
Key is pure love.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.063
So I added white flowers to it.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.601
It’s so cute.

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:47.204
It’s in a minimal style.

00:07:47.229 --> 00:07:49.524
Minimal. That’s so cute.

00:07:49.551 --> 00:07:53.200
I used one big flower
to represent blossoming love.

00:07:53.548 --> 00:07:54.845
These represent pure love.

00:07:54.872 --> 00:07:56.597
This represents cheerfulness.

00:07:56.625 --> 00:07:59.428
I keep it minimal because P’Chan
might have allergic reactions.

00:07:59.447 --> 00:08:01.730
That’s right. Key is very thoughtful.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.389
-The cake is so cute.
-Wow.

00:08:08.426 --> 00:08:10.302
What should we write on it?

00:08:10.712 --> 00:08:12.665
Right now, we are in
a cake decorating workshop.

00:08:12.697 --> 00:08:15.527
Earlier, we made cocktails
and arranged flowers for each other.

00:08:15.558 --> 00:08:16.527
Yes.

00:08:16.554 --> 00:08:19.528
This is the last session.

00:08:19.558 --> 00:08:21.077
Anniversary.

00:08:22.022 --> 00:08:24.100
Should we write Moonshadow something?

00:08:24.232 --> 00:08:26.001
Or Chan-Key something?

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.600
Chan loves Key and Chey loves Kan.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.550
[THAIS LOVES SPOONERISM.]
Chan loves Key and Chey loves Kan.

00:08:28.725 --> 00:08:31.801
Let’s write a clingy message
like Chan-Key Forever.

00:08:31.828 --> 00:08:32.989
Will it fit on the cake?

00:08:33.023 --> 00:08:33.931
Will it fit?

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.401
P’Mi, I’ll let you write Key.

00:08:51.217 --> 00:08:53.274
-Here is Chan.
-That’s cute.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.230
I don’t think we can write forever on it.
[JUST THE WORD ‘CHAN’
TOOK HALF OF THE SPACE.]

00:08:55.263 --> 00:08:56.388
Should we draw a heart instead?

00:08:56.416 --> 00:08:57.887
-A heart is good.
-P’Mi, you draw it.

00:09:02.668 --> 00:09:03.891
Then write Key.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.102
It looks a bit strange.

00:09:15.457 --> 00:09:17.514
Let’s decorate the cake.

00:09:20.154 --> 00:09:22.084
I haven’t done anything like this before:

00:09:22.115 --> 00:09:23.712
a cake decorating workshop.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:26.374
Now, there are many workshops we can join.

00:09:26.394 --> 00:09:29.032
Do you remember
that I made a cake for you?

00:09:29.051 --> 00:09:30.065
Yes.

00:09:30.097 --> 00:09:33.915
I was surprised that
you did that kind of thing.

00:09:34.158 --> 00:09:35.540
That’s a good thing
about having a younger partner.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.982
She makes me feel young?

00:09:36.998 --> 00:09:38.722
P’Chan will feel younger.

00:09:38.743 --> 00:09:40.397
Get to try something new.

00:09:40.835 --> 00:09:43.195
Has Key ever taken you
to do any activities?

00:09:43.228 --> 00:09:44.896
Has she?

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:46.302
Key…

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.004
-Has she ever done it?
-Do you want to transform into a punk girl?

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:53.220
Key teaches P’Chan
how to dress like a punk girl.

00:09:53.251 --> 00:09:55.005
The cake workshop that I did last time.

00:09:55.035 --> 00:09:55.672
What about it?

00:09:55.696 --> 00:09:56.899
It was very expensive.

00:09:57.127 --> 00:09:59.200
-How much was it?
-But the delivery fee was even higher.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.900
Look at where my house is located.

00:10:01.325 --> 00:10:02.497
It’s so far.

00:10:02.724 --> 00:10:04.943
That day, you asked me
if I was going anywhere.

00:10:04.964 --> 00:10:06.616
You never asked me that.

00:10:06.645 --> 00:10:08.429
I thought it was weird
that you asked me that.

00:10:08.448 --> 00:10:10.100
I built a cake for you.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:11.902
It was unexpected.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:13.237
See?

00:10:13.266 --> 00:10:14.232
It made me feel spirited.

00:10:14.253 --> 00:10:15.825
-Right?
-Yes.

00:10:15.859 --> 00:10:19.751
It’s like having a kitten.

00:10:19.774 --> 00:10:20.998
A kitten?

00:10:21.441 --> 00:10:23.745
It makes my life feel more lively.

00:10:23.773 --> 00:10:25.745
Energetic.

00:10:25.985 --> 00:10:29.065
-The cake is so cute.
-I’ll put the sprinkles on it.

00:10:29.093 --> 00:10:30.299
Sprinkles.

00:10:30.831 --> 00:10:33.802
-The pink sprinkles.
-The blue sprinkles are also cute.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.391
Done.

00:10:39.413 --> 00:10:40.776
It’s so cute.

00:10:41.137 --> 00:10:43.500
P’Chan loves Key.

00:10:44.266 --> 00:10:45.500
Forever.

00:10:45.866 --> 00:10:48.311
We wanted to write forever too,
but it doesn’t have space left.

00:10:49.047 --> 00:10:51.988
It’s a lovely day, more than I expected.

00:10:52.059 --> 00:10:53.300
It’s like a vacation for us.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.120
Yes, it feels like a vacation.

00:10:55.146 --> 00:10:58.536
We haven’t had a big meal together
for some time.

00:10:58.562 --> 00:11:01.056
We didn’t do activities together
for a long time.

00:11:01.084 --> 00:11:03.487
All we do is work.

00:11:03.515 --> 00:11:05.622
It feels like a relaxing day.

00:11:05.645 --> 00:11:10.234
Yes, we get to relax, do many workshops,
and strengthen our bond.

00:11:10.605 --> 00:11:13.728
I haven’t joined a cake workshop before.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.367
We helped you
live your teenage days again.

00:11:16.394 --> 00:11:18.051
I never had a teenage life.

00:11:18.084 --> 00:11:22.263
An early Gen Z teen
meets a late Gen Z teen.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.490
That’s right.

00:11:23.518 --> 00:11:26.226
We took you to do Gen Z activities.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.546
Is this an activity
that Gen Z likes to do?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.011
-Yes, cake decorating.
-I have never done it before.

00:11:32.054 --> 00:11:33.604
I have never done it.

00:11:34.272 --> 00:11:36.601
Thank you so much, GMMTV.

00:11:36.825 --> 00:11:38.281
I said thank you so many times on this vlog.

00:11:38.305 --> 00:11:40.417
-I have never done these activities.
-Yes, this is fun.

00:11:40.445 --> 00:11:42.231
I have never made a cocktail before.

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.651
Me too.

00:11:43.681 --> 00:11:47.208
Don’t forget to check out
our series, Moonshadow.

00:11:47.237 --> 00:11:52.176
-The story is getting intense.
-The series is already halfway through.

00:11:52.205 --> 00:11:56.441
Let’s see what kind of ending is waiting
for each character.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:56.998
Yes.

00:11:57.017 --> 00:11:58.130
Let’s see what will happen next
in the series.

00:11:58.162 --> 00:12:01.063
If you want to do these activities like us,

00:12:01.088 --> 00:12:04.004
you can visit Baby Bar Bangkok.

00:12:04.032 --> 00:12:05.776
The place has a beautiful atmosphere.

00:12:05.801 --> 00:12:08.114
Many cute workshops are available to do.

00:12:08.133 --> 00:12:10.968
All the activities we did today
are available in one place.

00:12:10.994 --> 00:12:13.348
-Yes. It’s really cute.
-It has a great vibe.

00:12:13.374 --> 00:12:17.001
Don’t forget to visit Baby Bar Bangkok.

00:12:33.374 --> 00:12:34.250
Ready?

00:12:39.054 --> 00:12:41.000
-Can you take a picture for us?
-It’s a firecracker.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.096
Don’t sit near it. It’s scary.

00:12:44.125 --> 00:12:45.183
(That’s cute.)

00:12:49.229 --> 00:12:50.505
Will it reignite?

00:12:50.656 --> 00:12:51.598
Will it?

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:56.099
This is so Gen Z.

00:12:56.659 --> 00:12:58.496
Now, I get why people like it.

00:13:03.091 --> 00:13:04.496
-P’Chan.
-Yes.

00:13:06.577 --> 00:13:07.857
This is a flower from me.

00:13:07.888 --> 00:13:08.802
Thank you.

00:13:08.997 --> 00:13:09.903
Did you make it?

00:13:10.008 --> 00:13:12.500
Yes, but she helped me wrap it.

00:13:13.091 --> 00:13:14.354
The food looks tasty.

00:13:14.382 --> 00:13:16.853
-I made it myself.
-Oh my.

00:13:16.967 --> 00:13:19.397
You should be a chef instead of a singer.

00:13:20.647 --> 00:13:21.760
Let’s dig in.

00:13:21.785 --> 00:13:24.582
-Shall we?
-Yes.

00:13:24.829 --> 00:13:25.734
Bye.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.299
-Excuse us. We will go enjoy this meal.
-I had a great time today.

00:13:29.638 --> 00:13:30.598
I love my job.

